Deathtrap Native 50 @VERSION@
================================

Free unofficial modernization patch for the 32-bit Steam release of
Ian Livingstone's Deathtrap Dungeon (1998).

Developed using OpenAI Codex under human direction and validated through
extensive manual playtesting and automated tests.

Tested game:
https://store.steampowered.com/app/245010/Deathtrap_Dungeon/

Gameplay demo:
https://youtu.be/U1RjdVP49TQ

The complete user-facing list of changes is included in CHANGELOG.txt.

QUICK INSTALL

1. Close the game.
2. Download dgVoodoo2 2.86 or newer from:
   https://github.com/dege-diosg/dgVoodoo2/releases
3. Copy dgVoodooCpl.exe plus the x86 DDraw.dll and D3DImm.dll wrappers from
   the dgVoodoo2 package directly beside DD_CD.EXE. Do not use x64 wrappers.
   D3D9.dll is not required by Deathtrap Dungeon.
4. Run dgVoodooCpl.exe for the game directory. Set Output API to Direct3D 11
   feature level 11.0, apply it, and confirm that dgVoodoo.conf beside
   DD_CD.EXE contains:

       [General]
       OutputAPI = d3d11_fl11_0

5. Only after dgVoodoo2 is configured, extract every file from this patch ZIP
   directly beside DD_CD.EXE. Preserve the included payload directory.
6. Double-click INSTALL.cmd once. It validates dgVoodoo2 and the game, then
   backs up a previous patch installation, installs the new payload and merges
   the required controls into ASYLUM\keys.cfg without replacing the complete
   file.
7. Start Deathtrap Dungeon normally.

dgVoodoo2 is required for the supported patch. DINPUT.dll may load without it,
but the complete higher-rate rendering path is not expected to work correctly.

The tested Steam Dungeon.dll SHA-256 is:
95FE9CE0FFF387F00704548F152E4340815213FCB3833DBE1B5C42871E7D2E56

The tested Steam DD_CD.EXE SHA-256 is:
0C644A00E62652E046C5DAD2960F0F6C8C1998F4CA065780FBD7811D9908BF1F

The installer warns but continues if the game hashes differ. Untested game
files may be partially or completely incompatible.

MOUSE AND KEYBOARD

Mouse movement     Rotate modern camera / first-person look
Left mouse         Primary attack
Right mouse        Block or parry
Mouse wheel        Previous/next available melee weapon
W / S              Walk forward/backward
Shift + W / S      Run forward/backward
A / D              Turn left/right
Shift + A / D      Fast turn left/right
J / K              Side-step left/right
Ctrl + W / S       Step forward/backward
Ctrl + A / D       Original side-step left/right
Space              Jump or climb
Space + direction  Directional jump
F                  Ranged attack / original combat modifier
F + W/A/D          Original directional melee attacks
F + S              Original parry
Q                  Cast/use selected spell
E                  Operate or interact
F1 / F2 / F3 / F4 Melee / ranged / spell-shield / consumable selector
1-8                Choose slot in an opened retail item selector
Tab                Original retail first-person view
F10                Body-visible immersive first-person view
F11                Toggle approximately 50 FPS native presentation
I                  Inventory
Esc                Open or leave menu
O / P              Save/load game

Immersive first person uses A/D for pure full-speed side movement. Combine
W/S with A/D for diagonals and hold Shift to run.

XBOX-COMPATIBLE CONTROLLER

Left stick         Camera-relative movement; full tilt runs / menu navigation
Right stick        Camera or first-person look / menu pointer / radial choice
A                  Jump or climb / confirm / skip supported screens
B                  Back in menus
X                  Operate or interact / alternate screen skip
Y                  Unassigned
RT                 Primary attack
LT                 Block or parry
RB                 Cast/use contextual spell action
LB + left stick    Original side-step movement
Start/Menu         Open pause menu / leave menu
R3                 Original retail first-person view
View/Back          Body-visible immersive first-person view
D-pad tap          Cycle next item in the selected category
D-pad hold         Open radial selector; choose with right stick

D-pad categories: up melee, right ranged, down spells/shields, left
potions/charms.

PROJECTS AND REPOSITORIES USED

MinHook 1.3.4 - statically linked API-hooking dependency:
https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook

dgVoodoo2 - required external DirectDraw/D3DImm runtime:
https://github.com/dege-diosg/dgVoodoo2

Unity Cinemachine - camera design reference; no code included:
https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/com.unity.cinemachine

UE Explorer - Arkham Asylum camera research tool; no code included:
https://github.com/UE-Explorer/UE-Explorer

ogg-winmm - Steam music-routing research reference; not included or required:
https://github.com/bangstk/ogg-winmm

The installer creates a timestamped backup of ASYLUM\keys.cfg under the
game's back directory. Do not copy a complete keys.cfg from another install.

This patch contains no game assets and no dgVoodoo files. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
must remain with redistributed copies of the patch.

